WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:33.440
I told you on Monday that 105 house Democrats
now publicly support and impeachment inquiry

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:38.750
against Donald Trump, that number has increased
and the House Democrats have now reached and

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:43.390
surpassed the 50% mark to get to an impeachment
inquiry.

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:51.129
The house. 435 members, half plus one is 218
the number of Democrats now supporting and

00:00:51.129 --> 00:00:56.550
impeachment inquiry is at least one oh nine
exactly half of that to 18 and according to

00:00:56.550 --> 00:01:03.119
some reports it's as high as 117 including
the support of former Republican congressman

00:01:03.119 --> 00:01:08.830
Justin Amash, who we have talked about is
abandoning the Republican Party for very good

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:14.620
reasons that a m indicate his concern with
what's going on there. So remember, Republicans

00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:19.979
are not needed to reach 50% plus one support
because Democrats took control of the house

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:26.110
in the 2018 midterms. Another one of the ways
in which that election was extremely important

00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:30.380
and every election is important. Now there
are a few things that are continuing to hold

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:35.690
this number back. Why is there not more support
for an impeachment inquiry in the House of

00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:40.260
Representatives? Number one, if Nancy Pelosi,
the democratic speaker of the House said,

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:46.420
yeah, it's time, it's time to start the impeachment
inquiry, that would instantly increase support

00:01:46.420 --> 00:01:48.760
among Democrats in the House of Representatives.

00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:54.600
Secondly, there are Democrats in red states
who are worried about the consequences in

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:59.860
their 2020 reelection campaigns. If they support
an impeachment inquiry that their constituents

00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:04.600
don't like, I do not think that this is a
real issue. The power of incumbency is going

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:09.619
to be outdone by simply standing up for what
you believe in or let me kind of frame it

00:02:09.619 --> 00:02:16.849
a different way. If a Republican can knock
out an incumbent Democrat simply by saying

00:02:16.849 --> 00:02:22.010
the Democrat is bad because they wanted an
impeachment inquiry, that's not a Democrat

00:02:22.010 --> 00:02:27.640
who has a very strong hold of their district
to begin with, so I don't buy that nonsense

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:31.450
for even a second. And then there's one other
important thing to remember, which is that

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:37.220
half of House Democrats or a little more now
publicly support and impeachment inquiry.

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:43.560
Of course there are more who support it privately,
but for different reasons have not yet decided

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:44.560
to go public.

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:47.870
It could be for the reasons I mentioned before,
it could be for reasons I haven't mentioned.

00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:53.319
The number one oh nine is noteworthy or one
17 or whatever the number is. It's noteworthy

00:02:53.319 --> 00:02:58.880
both for how large it is and for how small
it is. What I mean by that is on the one hand,

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:04.340
it's not common for half of the members of
one party in Congress to want to start an

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:08.510
impeachment inquiry against the president.
When Barack Obama was president, you didn't

00:03:08.510 --> 00:03:12.571
have half of House Republicans wanting an
impeachment inquiry against them because it

00:03:12.571 --> 00:03:17.569
wouldn't have made any sense. With George
W. Bush, you didn't have half of Democrats

00:03:17.569 --> 00:03:22.239
wanting to start an impeachment inquiry against
George W. Bush and he did some really, really

00:03:22.239 --> 00:03:28.520
bad things. So this is a very large number
in the sense that it's trouble for Donald

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:35.099
Trump, but there's another side to that. How
is it that only one oh nine or one 17 members

00:03:35.099 --> 00:03:38.670
of congress are publicly foreign impeachment
inquiry?

00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:44.140
Given everything that we have already learned,
all that to happen is Nancy Pelosi saying,

00:03:44.140 --> 00:03:50.180
I believe we need to start an impeachment
inquiry. If she does that, it's over. It's

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:58.320
already unusual to see 109 or 117 break with
the public view of the speaker of the house

00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:02.970
from their own party. If Pelosi comes around,
we will have an impeachment inquiry. In the

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:07.580
end, she should come around because it's the
right thing to do and it's her job. The only

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:13.640
good argument I have heard for not starting
an impeachment inquiry today is the idea that

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:17.470
starting an in six months might be more damaging
to Donald Trump, and I would be okay with

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:22.860
that. Short of that explanation, I don't see
any reason not to start an impeachment inquiry

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:27.990
immediately. And I want to hear from you about
it. Make sure that you're following the David

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:29.380
Pakman show on [inaudible]

00:04:29.380 --> 00:04:35.039
Instagram at David Pakman show. And while
you're there, throw me a follow as well at

